\section{Overview}
Apex-TI is a fully software-defined quantum--topological simulation framework
featuring autonomous solver intelligence, distributed tensor fabrics, compiler-
optimized sparse kernels, and a complete virtual quantum substrate (VQS).
The system operates without hardware constraints, enabling multi-scale physics
experiments entirely in virtualized memory.

\section{Core Components}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{Apex-TI v2.1 Autonomous Solver Intelligence} — Dynamic solver switching, adaptive tolerances, and self-healing density matrix rollback.
    \item \textbf{Apex-TI v3.1 Autonomous Cluster Intelligence} — Predictive shard migration, decentralized synchronization, and fault-tolerant distributed execution.
    \item \textbf{Apex-TI v4.0 Virtual Quantum Substrate} — Multi-scale tensor engine, deterministic time-reversal checkpoints, and zero-hardware emulation.
    \item \textbf{ApexIR Compiler Suite} — MLIR-style intermediate representation with optimization passes for sparse tensor contraction and topological invariant folding.
\end{itemize}

